			"Message": "build(deps): bump zod from 4.4.1 to 4.4.2\n\nBumps [zod](https://github.com/colinhacks/zod) from 4.4.1 to 4.4.2.\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/colinhacks/zod/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/colinhacks/zod/compare/v4.4.1...v4.4.2)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: zod\n  dependency-version: 4.4.2\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-patch\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>",
			"SHA": "5bc2b3b132b727c793cbb5e4e6028dd184960d12"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T00:14:42Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				105,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Sky): Implement placeholder registry for webview creation\n\nIntroduce a handler for `sky://webview/create` to park placeholder objects under their handle in the `__CEL_WEBVIEW_VIEWS_BY_HANDLE__` registry. Previously, extension-initiated panel creation from Cocoon lacked a Sky-side target, causing subsequent `webview/set-html` calls to fail silently when the registry lookup returned undefined.\n\nThe placeholder mimics the `webview` interface properties (html setter/getter), allowing HTML updates to queue as `_pendingHtml` without throwing errors before the `IWebviewWorkbenchService` is fully wired in the workbench service layer. Add conditional first-time logging for the creation event to aid diagnostics without saturating the IPC channel during boot.\n\nThis ensures robust initialization of panel-mode webviews even when the workbench accessor is not yet available, preventing silent drops of content updates during extension boot.",
			"SHA": "871cb8d522b9cb63365751205d23f78d3bfe9fd1"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T00:14:39Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				105,
				1
			],
			"Message": "perf(Sky): Optimize bridge logging and support decoration batching\n\nRefactor diagnostic bridges to log only on first successful push or resolution, preventing IPC saturation during LSP boot and heavy rendering. The `Markers.changeOne`, `webview/set-html`, and webview resolution paths now emit a single confirmation log with key triage data (URI, severity, length, handle match) and remain silent thereafter. Replace per-fire traces with conditional one-time logs guarded by state flags.\n\nUpdate decoration handlers to accept batched payloads from Mountain's coalesced lifecycle notifications (`Vine`), demultiplexing them into standard DOM events so individual listeners remain simple. Extend webview lookup to support handle-based resolution for panel-mode webviews lacking `viewId`, ensuring robust HTML application.\n\nThis restores keystroke responsiveness during extension boot and reduces channel noise while preserving essential debug data for the first occurrence of each bridge type.",
			"SHA": "9fc71928a7bc7fb1fd48d85457d42cd7706d331b"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-01T03:15:31Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				105,
				1
			],
			"Message": "Merge branch 'Current' of ssh://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Sky into Current",
